From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:43:29 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(doctor): seventh review round - -u for any program,
 bracketed/OData query names, values cut at "&"

- the generic -u/--user user:pass rule applies to every program again, except
  programs whose -u names a user or user:group (ps, docker, sudo, ...)
- query names are percent-decoded, may start with "$" (OData), and are split
  at brackets before the secret-name check (user[password], token[])
- a masked query value carries masking into the malformed pieces after it;
  encoded query values are decoded before they are judged
- a leading "!" is a glob only after a glob flag (rg -g, --exclude=)
- query_value fuzz position; tests pin the masking carry

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hermes_state_argv_secrets.py            | 73 +++++++++++++++-----
 tests/hermes_state/test_argv_secrets.py | 88 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 144 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

